   "text": "I read the drawing region by region and wrote the SMILES from that. The ring-closure digits and the stereodescriptors were checked by hand, not by software.\n\n**Skeleton**\n- **Macrocycle ester:** a piperazic acid (hexahydropyridazine) ring whose C3 carries the C(=O)O ester. The ester oxygen is linked through CH2\u2013C(CH3)2\u2013CH2 to indole C3.\n- **Indole:** N-ethyl, with a 2-substituent that is a pyridin-3-yl ring carrying a CH(CH3)OCH3 group at its 2-position. Indole C5 is bonded to thiazole C4.\n- **Thiazole to piperazic N:** thiazole C2 is linked by CH2\u2013CH(NH\u2013C(=O)\u2013cyclobutyl)\u2013C(=O) to the piperazic ring N1, which closes the macrocycle.\n- **Cyclobutane:** the amide carbonyl is on one ring carbon, and a nitrile is on the adjacent carbon.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\nThe five stereocentres are labelled (S) in the drawing. I worked out the CIP priorities at each centre and chose @ or @@ in the SMILES to give S:\n- piperazic C3 (S)\n- the alpha carbon bearing the amide NH (S)\n- the cyclobutane carbon bearing the amide carbonyl (S)\n- the cyclobutane carbon bearing the nitrile (S)\n- the CH(CH3)OCH3 carbon on the pyridine (S)\n\nSMILES: O=C1OCC(C)(C)Cc2c(-c3cccnc3[C@H](C)OC)n(CC)c3ccc(cc23)-c2csc(n2)C[C@H](NC(=O)[C@H]2CC[C@@H]2C#N)C(=O)N2CCC[C@@H]1N2"
